# Mana Drain: "Counter target spell. At the beginning of your next main phase, add an amount of {C} equal to that
# spell's mana value." Mind Twist cast for X=2 ({X}{B}) has mana value 3 while it is on the stack, and Mana Drain uses
# that value as the spell was when it was countered (CR 608.2h; CR 202.3e: X is as chosen on the stack). Bot2 casts
# it on turn 2 with Black Lotus; Bot1 counters it, and in its precombat main phase of turn 3 has {C}{C}{C}, not {C}.

